/// `parenthesized_product`: the retired product type `(A, B)`. The telescope
/// `*{A, B}` replaces it. The lowering refuses the list at its first comma, and
/// the refusal names it. The domain `(A, B) -> C` and the outputs `-> (A, B)`
/// keep their readings.
@[refuses("RetiredSpelling.parenthesized_product")]
def p : (Integer, String);
